FFmpeg is a submodule, not part of this repository
--------------------------------------------------

`FFmpeg/` is a git submodule. Clone without `--recursive` and it is not there at all. Its contents
are licensed by the FFmpeg project, not by this one, and how they are licensed depends on how you
configure the build.

The configuration used here — see the *Make FFmpeg* build phase — passes `--enable-gpl` and
`--enable-version3`, which makes the resulting FFmpeg libraries **GPL v3**. Without those flags
FFmpeg builds under the LGPL.


x264 and x265 are fetched at build time
---------------------------------------

The build copies `libx264.a` and `libx265.a` out of Homebrew. They are **GPL v2 or later**, are not
redistributed in this repository, and are only present if you build with `--enable-libx264` and
`--enable-libx265`.


A built FFmpegTask binary is GPL v3
-----------------------------------

This is the one that has consequences. FFmpegTask statically links FFmpeg, x264 and x265, so the
**binary** is a combined work and must be distributed under the GPL — regardless of the MIT licence
on the sources that went into it. Shipping `XPCFFmpegService.xpc` inside an application means
distributing that binary, with the obligations that carries: preserve the notices, ship the licence
text, and make the corresponding source available. This repository, being public, is that source.

Nothing else built from this repository contains FFmpeg code. The application, the XPC service and
`XPCFFmpeg.framework` have zero FFmpeg symbols, which you can check for yourself:

    nm -U YourApp.app/Contents/MacOS/YourApp | grep -cE '_av_|_avcodec_|_x264_|_x265_'   # 0

That separation is deliberate, and it is why an application using this service does not have to
publish its own source. The reasoning is in FFmpegTask/README.md.

If you would rather not ship GPL code at all, build FFmpeg without `--enable-gpl`,
`--enable-version3`, `--enable-libx264` and `--enable-libx265`, and use the VideoToolbox encoders.
The MIT sources here are unchanged by that choice; only what they link against changes.
